/* The primary's SCPI command tree of z3801a-3543.bin as C data: its tree pair,
 * the common commands' list and the main tree, and every record they reach,
 * each of the type third_party/firmware/z3801a-3543/smartclock.h declares and
 * reproducing the image's bytes but for its pointers. Generated by `make
 * scpi-tree` (smartclock-cli dump-scpi --c --names-file names.tsv
 * z3801a-3543.bin, then clang-format); do not edit by hand.
 * docs/scpi/README.md, "As C", gives the names; a field left out is zero.  A
 * record's pointer is cast to its field's type, since the records are const and
 * the fields are not: Ghidra's types, which the exported C compiles this with,
 * keep no const.  A converter's and a formatter's are cast too, their
 * prototypes not the field's own; a handler's is not.  A child list's children
 * are an array of their own, which follows the list as in the
 * image.  Each record but a string is aligned to an even address,
 * as the image's are, since a word or a long at an odd one is
 * misaligned (MC68331UM, 4.4.4) and the types are packed.  Defining
 * SCPI_TREE_DATA_ALONE declares the routines, to compile the file alone. */

